  "why": {
    "tokens": [
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "Stock is often spread over several warehouses, and a warehouse's name doesn't tell you what it holds. This view shows one row for each warehouse that knows the item, with or without stock, so you can choose by the numbers. "
      },
      {
        "t": "field",
        "v": "Economic Stock"
      },
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " on each row is on-hand plus on-order minus allocated. It goes below zero when other orders need more than the warehouse has or expects."
      }
    ],
